=== Setup ===
null: 30 random splits of the real sample (n = 5068)
planted: 20 replications at each of 7 shift sizes, 2,500 per group
cores: 10,  nominal alpha: 0.05 after Benjamini-Hochberg

=== 1. Null: random splits of the real respondents ===
Split the sample at random into two groups. Nothing distinguishes them, so
the correct number of flagged items is zero and every flag is an error.
Many splits, not one, because a single split is a sample of size one.

