=== 2. Null with impact but no DIF ===
A random split gives two groups identical in every way. The case that
actually arises is two groups that genuinely differ in depression while
the items behave identically, which is the CFA's 0.19 SD sex difference
with no measurement bias at all. Group mean differences are a known way to
induce spurious DIF, so the random split alone would understate the rate.

