Read the first and last row of each block. That slope, not the level, is
the contamination: how much a procedure's false-alarm rate on innocent
items is driven by how many guilty items are in the questionnaire with
them. It is the difference between a test of one item and a test of the
company that item keeps.

  all_other  0.006 with no DIF present -> 0.870 with 4 items carrying it (+0.864)
  anchored   0.000 with no DIF present -> 0.267 with 4 items carrying it (+0.267)
  lordif     0.033 with no DIF present -> 0.900 with 4 items carrying it (+0.867)

And purification is not free: with 4 guilty items, an average of 1.20
of them ended up inside the anchor set, where they are never tested and
are instead defining the scale every other item is judged against.

